app.get('/conservation-audit', async (c) => {

The block to delete ends at that second handler's own closing `});`, which is immediately followed by a blank line and then this line, which also occurs EXACTLY ONCE in the file:

app.post('/conservation-audit-emit', async (c) => {

ONE OPERATION. Delete the entire second `app.get('/conservation-audit', ...)` handler — from the `app.get` line identified by the no-blank-line boundary above, through its matching closing `});` — so that the first handler's closing `});` is followed by a blank line and then `app.post('/conservation-audit-emit', async (c) => {`.

After the change the file must contain EXACTLY ONE occurrence of `app.get('/conservation-audit'`, and must still contain exactly one occurrence each of `app.post('/conservation-audit-emit'` and `app.get('/conservation-residual-trend'`. Do not modify the surviving handler's body, and do not touch the emit or residual-trend routes — they are distinct, correct routes.

